+// for OB64 is 60 buffers/s of 552 frames while the DAC plays 32000 frames/s —
+// a 3.5% overproduction that grows the output queue by ~2 s a minute.
+//
+// On hardware the game polls this bit in a tight loop (the CPU is fast relative
+// to one buffer), so "busy while anything is still playing" is enough. In the
+// recompiled port the same loop only iterates ~120 times/s — coarser than one
+// 17 ms buffer — so clearing the bit exactly when the queue empties makes the
+// game generate one buffer *late*: measured with a queue-depth probe it produced
